==Battleground==
*3 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Blanka (Enemy)|Blanka]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
**3 [[Kang Roo]]s spawn, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
**1 [[Dhalsim (Enemy)|Dhalsim]] spawns.

==Strategy==
A strategy you can do at the start is kill the Squire Rel and stall the Kang Roo if you are not going for rewards. Since no enemies spawn after the third Squire Rel, this could help you prepare for the boss wave.

When you are ready to attack, send 1 cat that can hit the base and act as bait, do not spawn any meatshields yet. Then when the boss wave is activated, let them kill the cat and lure Blanka to your base. Once Blanka is close, summon some meatshields (level 20 [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]] is enough, then summon all your other cats and kill Blanka. If you cannot kill Blanka before Dhalsim gets there then Dhalsim will make it a bit harder since he can weaken your cats. Try to kill the Kang Roos for money and you should be alright once both Blanka and Dhalsim are dead. You can also just attack them head on. This is also a viable strategy.

Cats that can outrange Blanka and Dhalsim like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] are useful when trying to beat the stage. You can also try to spam Giraffe Cats if they are high enough level. Treasures also help.

